# Killing the last player must end the round, not crash
#
# What this covers: RenderSpritesWithShaders collected raw component pointers
# in for_each_with and rendered them from once(). SystemManager::render calls
# once() *before* the entity loop (core/system.h:513), so it was always drawing
# the previous frame's batch -- fine until an entity is destroyed between
# frames, at which point every pointer in it dangles. Eliminating a player is
# the first thing in the game that destroys a kart, so this was unreachable
# until CheckLivesWinFFA's solo-round guard landed. Before the fix this script
# segfaults in HasShader::has_shader.
#
# What this does NOT cover: the MatchKartsToPlayers menu-only guard, added in
# the same change. Verified by reverting it -- all 14 still pass. With no
# gamepad connected ProvidesMaxGamepadID::count() is 1, so once the only player
# dies "size() + 1 == count()" is true and the function returns before it can
# rebuild anyone. Reaching that path needs at least two eliminations, so at
# least two karts, and e2e spawns exactly one. Left uncovered rather than
# faked.
#
# No screenshots: the kart is live and moving.

disable_animations

set_round_type Lives
goto_screen Main
wait 0.2

start_round
wait_frames 2
expect_state Playing
expect_tracker lives 1

# Lives 1 -> 0 -> the kart is destroyed.
set_tracker health 0
wait_frames 10

expect_state Menu

goto_screen Main
wait 0.2
